Watchtower patch (#603, owner-approved in ask #494) to the SQLCipher v4.19.0
amalgamation, applied by scripts/sqlcipher-amalgamation.sh.

ATTACH with no key (VACUUM's temporary database, VACUUM INTO, a plain
ATTACH) attached a SQLCipher codec whenever the main database had reserved
bytes per page. A plaintext main database with reserved bytes (macOS's
system SQLite writes 12) then had a keyless codec attach fail, and VACUUM
returned "unable to open database". The codec is now attached on reserved
bytes only when the main database itself has a codec. Pinned by
TestEngine_CompactPlaintextWithReservedBytes (internal/db).

--- a/internal/sqlcipher/sqlite3-binding.c
+++ b/internal/sqlcipher/sqlite3-binding.c
@@ -131775,7 +131775,12 @@
         rc = sqlite3CodecQueryParameters(db, zName, zPath, &seen);
         if( rc==SQLITE_OK && seen==0 ){
           sqlcipherCodecGetKey(db, 0, (void**)&zKey, &nKey);
-          if( nKey || sqlite3BtreeGetRequestedReserve(db->aDb[0].pBt)>0 ){
+          /* WATCHTOWER PATCH (#603): attach a codec on reserved bytes only
+          ** when the main database has one, so a plaintext main database
+          ** with reserved bytes (macOS SQLite writes 12) can VACUUM and
+          ** ATTACH without a key. See internal/sqlcipher/patches/. */
+          if( nKey || (sqlite3BtreeGetRequestedReserve(db->aDb[0].pBt)>0
+                       && sqlcipherPagerGetCodec(sqlite3BtreePager(db->aDb[0].pBt))!=0) ){
             rc = sqlcipherCodecAttach(db, db->nDb-1, zKey, nKey);
           }
           if(nKey) sqlcipher_free(zKey, nKey);
